      "skos:note": "Inserts new offences against torture, sexual image abuse, female genital mutilation, and sexual servitude."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-amendment-strengthening-the-criminal-justice-response-to-sexual-violence-act-2024#sch-1-sec-6",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "6 After paragraph 15Y(2)(b)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 8,
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n(bd) an offence against Division 274 of the Criminal Code\n(torture);\n(bi) an offence against any of the following arising under\nsection 6 of the Crimes at Sea Act 2000:\n(i) Part 3 (Sexual offences) of the Crimes Act 1900 (ACT);\n(ii) Part 3A (Intimate image abuse) of the Crimes Act 1900\n(ACT);\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\n\nNo. 114, 2024\nCrimes Amendment (Strengthening the Criminal Justice Response to\nSexual Violence) Act 2024\n(iii) Part 4 (Female genital mutilation) of the Crimes Act\n1900 (ACT);\n(iv) Part 5 (Sexual servitude) of the Crimes Act 1900 (ACT);\n(bj) an offence against section 14 or 15 of the Crimes (Aviation)\nAct 1991 arising under any of the following:\n(i) Part 3 (Sexual offences) of the Crimes Act 1900 (ACT);\n(ii) Part 3A (Intimate image abuse) of the Crimes Act 1900\n(ACT);\n(iii) Part 4 (Female genital mutilation) of the Crimes Act\n1900 (ACT);\n(iv) Part 5 (Sexual servitude) of the Crimes Act 1900 (ACT);\n(bk) an aggravated offence against Subdivision C of Division 12\nof Part 2 of the Migration Act 1958;\n(bl) a sexual offence specified in the regulations;"
    },
