          "@id": "concept:crimes-amendment-strengthening-the-criminal-justice-response-to-sexual-violence-act-2024-sch-1-sec-17a-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c1a9e807ecf33ae8eb7949f09ca5b504308ef5af48cd54588c4c1469a734000f"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-amendment-strengthening-the-criminal-justice-response-to-sexual-violence-act-2024#sch-1-sec-17a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "17A After section 15YAB",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 10,
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n15YAC  Child complainants\n(1) A child complainant, in relation to a child proceeding:\n(a) is a child who is, or is alleged to be, a victim of an offence, of\na kind referred to in subsection 15Y(1), to which the\nproceeding relates (whether or not the child is involved in the\nproceeding or was involved in the initiation of the\nproceeding); and\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\n\nNo. 114, 2024\nCrimes Amendment (Strengthening the Criminal Justice Response to\nSexual Violence) Act 2024\n(b) includes a person who was such a child at the time the\noffence concerned was alleged to have been committed.\n(2) However, a person who is 18 or over is not a child complainant if\nthe person informs the court that the person does not wish to be\ntreated as such a complainant.\n15YAD  Child witnesses\n(1) A child witness, in relation to a child proceeding:\n(a) is a child (including a child complainant) who is a witness in\nthe proceeding; and\n(b) includes a witness in the proceeding who was a child at the\ntime the offence concerned was alleged to have been\ncommitted.\n(2) However, a person who is 18 or over is not a child witness if the\nperson informs the court that the person does not wish to be treated\nas such a witness."
    },
