    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-amendment-strengthening-the-criminal-justice-response-to-sexual-violence-act-2024-sch-1-sec-32",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "32 At the end of Division 4 of Part IAD",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-amendment-strengthening-the-criminal-justice-response-to-sexual-violence-act-2024#sch-1-sec-32"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-amendment-strengthening-the-criminal-justice-response-to-sexual-violence-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-amendment-strengthening-the-criminal-justice-response-to-sexual-violence-act-2024.pdf, p.19",
      "values:originalText": "Add:\n15YLA  Recording of evidence given in person\n(1) The court must order that evidence given in person by a person to\nwhom subsection (2) applies is to be recorded if:\n(a) the court is satisfied that the evidence could be used in\nanother proceeding; and\n(b) the court is equipped with the necessary facilities; and\n(c) the person agrees to the evidence being recorded.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments\n\nCrimes Amendment (Strengthening the Criminal Justice Response to\nSexual Violence) Act 2024\nNo. 114, 2024\n(2) This subsection applies to the following persons:\n(a) for a child proceeding—a child witness;\n(b) for a vulnerable adult proceeding—a vulnerable adult\ncomplainant;\n(c) for a special witness proceeding—a special witness for whom\nan order under subsection 15YAB(3) is in force for this\nsection.\n(3) The recording may be a video or audio recording.\n(4) Subsection (1) applies whether or not the evidence is given by\nclosed-circuit television.",
      "skos:definition": "Add:\n15YLA  Recording of evidence given in person\n(1) The court must order that evidence given in person by a person to\nwhom subsection (2) applies is to be recorded if:\n(a) the court is satisfied that the evidence could be used in\nanother proceeding; and\n(b) the court is equipped with the necessary facilities; and\n(c) the person agrees to the evidence being recorded.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments\n\nCrimes Amendment (Strengthening the Criminal Justice Response to\nSexual Violence) Act 2024\nNo. 114, 2024\n(2) This subsection applies to the following persons:\n(a) for a child proceeding—a child witness;\n(b) for a vulnerable adult proceeding—a vulnerable adult\ncomplainant;\n(c) for a special witness proceeding—a special witness for whom\nan order under subsection 15YAB(3) is in force for this\nsection.\n(3) The recording may be a video or audio recording.\n(4) Subsection (1) applies whether or not the evidence is given by\nclosed-circuit television.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-amendment-strengthening-the-criminal-justice-response-to-sexual-violence-act-2024-sch-1-sec-32-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-amendment-strengthening-the-criminal-justice-response-to-sexual-violence-act-2024-sch-1-sec-32-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-amendment-strengthening-the-criminal-justice-response-to-sexual-violence-act-2024-sch-1-sec-32-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-amendment-strengthening-the-criminal-justice-response-to-sexual-violence-act-2024-sch-1-sec-32-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a660dfca8e7e23a7192aaeb1a3be7d8c11579143eec7fe769bc8dccd0b7f721c"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-amendment-strengthening-the-criminal-justice-response-to-sexual-violence-act-2024#sch-1-sec-32",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "32 At the end of Division 4 of Part IAD",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 19,
      "values:originalText": "Add:\n15YLA  Recording of evidence given in person\n(1) The court must order that evidence given in person by a person to\nwhom subsection (2) applies is to be recorded if:\n(a) the court is satisfied that the evidence could be used in\nanother proceeding; and\n(b) the court is equipped with the necessary facilities; and\n(c) the person agrees to the evidence being recorded.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments\n\nCrimes Amendment (Strengthening the Criminal Justice Response to\nSexual Violence) Act 2024\nNo. 114, 2024\n(2) This subsection applies to the following persons:\n(a) for a child proceeding—a child witness;\n(b) for a vulnerable adult proceeding—a vulnerable adult\ncomplainant;\n(c) for a special witness proceeding—a special witness for whom\nan order under subsection 15YAB(3) is in force for this\nsection.\n(3) The recording may be a video or audio recording.\n(4) Subsection (1) applies whether or not the evidence is given by\nclosed-circuit television."
    },
