    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-amendment-strengthening-the-criminal-justice-response-to-sexual-violence-act-2024-sch-1-sec-37",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "37 At the end of section 15YM",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-amendment-strengthening-the-criminal-justice-response-to-sexual-violence-act-2024#sch-1-sec-37"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-amendment-strengthening-the-criminal-justice-response-to-sexual-violence-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-amendment-strengthening-the-criminal-justice-response-to-sexual-violence-act-2024.pdf, p.20",
      "values:originalText": "Add:\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\n\nNo. 114, 2024\nCrimes Amendment (Strengthening the Criminal Justice Response to\nSexual Violence) Act 2024\nOffence\n(5) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person:\n(i) makes a recording (or other copy) of a recording, or a\npart of a recording, to which subsection (1) applies; or\n(ii) does anything (whether directly or indirectly) to damage\nor alter a recording, or a part of a recording, to which\nsubsection (1) applies; or\n(iii) possesses or supplies a recording, or a part of a\nrecording, to which subsection (1) applies; or\n(iv) possesses or supplies a copy of a recording, or a part of\na recording, to which subsection (1) applies; and\n(b) the person does so without lawful authority or excuse.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 60 penalty units, or both.\n(6) The fault element for paragraph (5)(a) is intention.",
      "skos:definition": "Add:\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\n\nNo. 114, 2024\nCrimes Amendment (Strengthening the Criminal Justice Response to\nSexual Violence) Act 2024\nOffence\n(5) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person:\n(i) makes a recording (or other copy) of a recording, or a\npart of a recording, to which subsection (1) applies; or\n(ii) does anything (whether directly or indirectly) to damage\nor alter a recording, or a part of a recording, to which\nsubsection (1) applies; or\n(iii) possesses or supplies a recording, or a part of a\nrecording, to which subsection (1) applies; or\n(iv) possesses or supplies a copy of a recording, or a part of\na recording, to which subsection (1) applies; and\n(b) the person does so without lawful authority or excuse.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 60 penalty units, or both.\n(6) The fault element for paragraph (5)(a) is intention.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-amendment-strengthening-the-criminal-justice-response-to-sexual-violence-act-2024-sch-1-sec-37-ss-5"
