    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-amendment-strengthening-the-criminal-justice-response-to-sexual-violence-act-2024-sch-1-sec-50",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "50 After section 15YO",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-amendment-strengthening-the-criminal-justice-response-to-sexual-violence-act-2024#sch-1-sec-50"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-amendment-strengthening-the-criminal-justice-response-to-sexual-violence-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-amendment-strengthening-the-criminal-justice-response-to-sexual-violence-act-2024.pdf, p.22",
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n15YOA  Right to interpreter\n(1) If the court is satisfied that a person to whom subsection (2) applies\nis unable, because of inadequate knowledge of the English\nlanguage or a disability, to communicate orally with reasonable\nfluency in that language, the court must arrange for the presence of\nan interpreter to assist the person to understand, and participate in,\nthe proceeding.\n(2) This subsection applies to the following persons:\n(a) for a child proceeding—a child witness;\n(b) for a vulnerable adult proceeding—a vulnerable adult\ncomplainant;\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\n\nNo. 114, 2024\nCrimes Amendment (Strengthening the Criminal Justice Response to\nSexual Violence) Act 2024\n(c) for a special witness proceeding—a special witness for whom\nan order under subsection 15YAB(3) is in force for this\nsection.",
      "skos:definition": "Insert:\n15YOA  Right to interpreter\n(1) If the court is satisfied that a person to whom subsection (2) applies\nis unable, because of inadequate knowledge of the English\nlanguage or a disability, to communicate orally with reasonable\nfluency in that language, the court must arrange for the presence of\nan interpreter to assist the person to understand, and participate in,\nthe proceeding.\n(2) This subsection applies to the following persons:\n(a) for a child proceeding—a child witness;\n(b) for a vulnerable adult proceeding—a vulnerable adult\ncomplainant;\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\n\nNo. 114, 2024\nCrimes Amendment (Strengthening the Criminal Justice Response to\nSexual Violence) Act 2024\n(c) for a special witness proceeding—a special witness for whom\nan order under subsection 15YAB(3) is in force for this\nsection.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-amendment-strengthening-the-criminal-justice-response-to-sexual-violence-act-2024-sch-1-sec-50-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-amendment-strengthening-the-criminal-justice-response-to-sexual-violence-act-2024-sch-1-sec-50-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b54c03b32189fd29a007e6331cf28e0212c9ed7d9f02a6c44d965cf79ae8d8ff"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-amendment-strengthening-the-criminal-justice-response-to-sexual-violence-act-2024#sch-1-sec-50",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "50 After section 15YO",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 22,
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n15YOA  Right to interpreter\n(1) If the court is satisfied that a person to whom subsection (2) applies\nis unable, because of inadequate knowledge of the English\nlanguage or a disability, to communicate orally with reasonable\nfluency in that language, the court must arrange for the presence of\nan interpreter to assist the person to understand, and participate in,\nthe proceeding.\n(2) This subsection applies to the following persons:\n(a) for a child proceeding—a child witness;\n(b) for a vulnerable adult proceeding—a vulnerable adult\ncomplainant;\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\n\nNo. 114, 2024\nCrimes Amendment (Strengthening the Criminal Justice Response to\nSexual Violence) Act 2024\n(c) for a special witness proceeding—a special witness for whom\nan order under subsection 15YAB(3) is in force for this\nsection."
    },
