    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-amendment-strengthening-the-criminal-justice-response-to-sexual-violence-act-2024-sch-1-sec-55",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "55 Subsection 15YR(2)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-amendment-strengthening-the-criminal-justice-response-to-sexual-violence-act-2024#sch-1-sec-55"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-amendment-strengthening-the-criminal-justice-response-to-sexual-violence-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-amendment-strengthening-the-criminal-justice-response-to-sexual-violence-act-2024.pdf, p.23",
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if:\n(a) the publication is in an official publication in the course of,\nand for the purpose of, the proceeding; or\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments\n\nCrimes Amendment (Strengthening the Criminal Justice Response to\nSexual Violence) Act 2024\nNo. 114, 2024\n(b) the publication is in a document prepared for use in particular\nlegal proceedings (whether or not the legal proceedings are a\nproceeding within the meaning of this Part); or\n(c) the vulnerable person is deceased; or\n(d) for a vulnerable person who is an adult:\n(i) the vulnerable person has given informed consent to the\npublication in accordance with subsection (2A); and\n(ii) the publication is in accordance with the limits, if any,\nset by the vulnerable person; and\n(iii) at the time the consent was given—the vulnerable\nperson had the decision-making capacity to give such\nconsent; or\n(e) for a vulnerable person who is a child:\n(i) the vulnerable person has given informed consent for\nthe publication; and\n(ii) the publication is in accordance with the limits, if any,\nset by the vulnerable person; and\n(iii) the consent was accompanied by a supporting statement\nin accordance with subsection (2B).\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (2) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code).\n(2A) A vulnerable person gives informed consent to a publication in\naccordance with this subsection if, at the time the person gives the\nconsent, the person:\n(a) understands the options available to the person (including\nthat the person is not required to give the consent); and\n(b) understands the consequences of giving the consent.\n(2B) A supporting statement must:\n(a) be in writing; and\n(b) be made by a person (the practitioner) who is:\n(i) a medical practitioner; or\n(ii) a person registered or licensed as a psychologist under a\nlaw of a State or Territory that provides for the\nregistration or licensing of psychologists; or\n(iii) a person prescribed by the regulations; and\n(c) include the following details:\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\n\nNo. 114, 2024\nCrimes Amendment (Strengthening the Criminal Justice Response to\nSexual Violence) Act 2024\n(i) the name, qualification and business address of the\npractitioner;\n(ii) the nature and duration of the professional relationship\nbetween the practitioner and the vulnerable person; and\n(d) state that the practitioner is of the opinion that the vulnerable\nperson understands:\n(i) what it means to be identified as a vulnerable person of\nthat kind; and\n(ii) the consequences of losing anonymity.",
      "skos:definition": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if:\n(a) the publication is in an official publication in the course of,\nand for the purpose of, the proceeding; or\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments\n\nCrimes Amendment (Strengthening the Criminal Justice Response to\nSexual Violence) Act 2024\nNo. 114, 2024\n(b) the publication is in a document prepared for use in particular\nlegal proceedings (whether or not the legal proceedings are a\nproceeding within the meaning of this Part); or\n(c) the vulnerable person is deceased; or\n(d) for a vulnerable person who is an adult:\n(i) the vulnerable person has given informed consent to the\npublication in accordance with subsection (2A); and\n(ii) the publication is in accordance with the limits, if any,\nset by the vulnerable person; and\n(iii) at the time the consent was given—the vulnerable\nperson had the decision-making capacity to give such\nconsent; or\n(e) for a vulnerable person who is a child:\n(i) the vulnerable person has given informed consent for\nthe publication; and\n(ii) the publication is in accordance with the limits, if any,\nset by the vulnerable person; and\n(iii) the consent was accompanied by a supporting statement\nin accordance with subsection (2B).\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (2) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code).\n(2A) A vulnerable person gives informed consent to a publication in\naccordance with this subsection if, at the time the person gives the\nconsent, the person:\n(a) understands the options available to the person (including\nthat the person is not required to give the consent); and\n(b) understands the consequences of giving the consent.\n(2B) A supporting statement must:\n(a) be in writing; and\n(b) be made by a person (the practitioner) who is:\n(i) a medical practitioner; or\n(ii) a person registered or licensed as a psychologist under a\nlaw of a State or Territory that provides for the\nregistration or licensing of psychologists; or\n(iii) a",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-amendment-strengthening-the-criminal-justice-response-to-sexual-violence-act-2024-sch-1-sec-55-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-amendment-strengthening-the-criminal-justice-response-to-sexual-violence-act-2024-sch-1-sec-55-ss-2a"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-amendment-strengthening-the-criminal-justice-response-to-sexual-violence-act-2024-sch-1-sec-55-ss-2b"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "fc61fc4a50e655d12b70c909f99174b3a8932dca19bfcf9d8128e3cad72db45b"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-amendment-strengthening-the-criminal-justice-response-to-sexual-violence-act-2024#sch-1-sec-55",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "55 Subsection 15YR(2)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 23,
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if:\n(a) the publication is in an official publication in the course of,\nand for the purpose of, the proceeding; or\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments\n\nCrimes Amendment (Strengthening the Criminal Justice Response to\nSexual Violence) Act 2024\nNo. 114, 2024\n(b) the publication is in a document prepared for use in particular\nlegal proceedings (whether or not the legal proceedings are a\nproceeding within the meaning of this Part); or\n(c) the vulnerable person is deceased; or\n(d) for a vulnerable person who is an adult:\n(i) the vulnerable person has given informed consent to the\npublication in accordance with subsection (2A); and\n(ii) the publication is in accordance with the limits, if any,\nset by the vulnerable person; and\n(iii) at the time the consent was given—the vulnerable\nperson had the decision-making capacity to give such\nconsent; or\n(e) for a vulnerable person who is a child:\n(i) the vulnerable person has given informed consent for\nthe publication; and\n(ii) the publication is in accordance with the limits, if any,\nset by the vulnerable person; and\n(iii) the consent was accompanied by a supporting statement\nin accordance with subsection (2B).\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (2) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code).\n(2A) A vulnerable person gives informed consent to a publication in\naccordance with this subsection if, at the time the person gives the\nconsent, the person:\n(a) understands the options available to the person (including\nthat the person is not required to give the consent); and\n(b) understands the consequences of giving the consent.\n(2B) A supporting statement must:\n(a) be in writing; and\n(b) be made by a person (the practitioner) who is:\n(i) a medical practitioner; or\n(ii) a person registered or licensed as a psychologist under a\nlaw of a State or Territory that provides for the\nregistration or licensing of psychologists; or\n(iii) a person prescribed by the regulations; and\n(c) include the following details:\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\n\nNo. 114, 2024\nCrimes Amendment (Strengthening the Criminal Justice Response to\nSexual Violence) Act 2024\n(i) the name, qualification and business address of the\npractitioner;\n(ii) the nature and duration of the professional relationship\nbetween the practitioner and the vulnerable person; and\n(d) state that the practitioner is of the opinion that the vulnerable\nperson understands:\n(i) what it means to be identified as a vulnerable person of\nthat kind; and\n(ii) the consequences of losing anonymity."
    },
    {
