    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-amendment-strengthening-the-criminal-justice-response-to-sexual-violence-act-2024-sch-1-sec-55-ss-2b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "55(2B) Subsection 15YR(2)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-amendment-strengthening-the-criminal-justice-response-to-sexual-violence-act-2024#sch-1-sec-55-ss-2b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-amendment-strengthening-the-criminal-justice-response-to-sexual-violence-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-amendment-strengthening-the-criminal-justice-response-to-sexual-violence-act-2024.pdf, p.23",
      "values:originalText": "(2B) A supporting statement must:\n(a) be in writing; and\n(b) be made by a person (the practitioner) who is:\n(i) a medical practitioner; or\n(ii) a person registered or licensed as a psychologist under a\nlaw of a State or Territory that provides for the\nregistration or licensing of psychologists; or\n(iii) a person prescribed by the regulations; and\n(c) include the following details:\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\n\nNo. 114, 2024\nCrimes Amendment (Strengthening the Criminal Justice Response to\nSexual Violence) Act 2024\n(i) the name, qualification and business address of the\npractitioner;\n(ii) the nature and duration of the professional relationship\nbetween the practitioner and the vulnerable person; and\n(d) state that the practitioner is of the opinion that the vulnerable\nperson understands:\n(i) what it means to be identified as a vulnerable person of\nthat kind; and\n(ii) the consequences of losing anonymity.",
      "skos:definition": "(2B) A supporting statement must:\n(a) be in writing; and\n(b) be made by a person (the practitioner) who is:\n(i) a medical practitioner; or\n(ii) a person registered or licensed as a psychologist under a\nlaw of a State or Territory that provides for the\nregistration or licensing of psychologists; or\n(iii) a person prescribed by the regulations; and\n(c) include the following details:\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\n\nNo. 114, 2024\nCrimes Amendment (Strengthening the Criminal Justice Response to\nSexual Violence) Act 2024\n(i) the name, qualification and business address of the\npractitioner;\n(ii) the nature and duration of the professional relationship\nbetween the practitioner and the vulnerable person; and\n(d) state that the practitioner is of the opinion that the vulnerable\nperson understands:\n(i) what it means to be identified as a vulnerable person of\nthat kind; and\n(ii) the consequences of losing anonymity.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-amendment-strengthening-the-criminal-justice-response-to-sexual-violence-act-2024-sch-1-sec-55"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-amendment-strengthening-the-criminal-justice-response-to-sexual-violence-act-2024-sch-1-sec-55-ss-2b-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-amendment-strengthening-the-criminal-justice-response-to-sexual-violence-act-2024-sch-1-sec-55-ss-2b-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-amendment-strengthening-the-criminal-justice-response-to-sexual-violence-act-2024-sch-1-sec-55-ss-2b-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "461f759c3dcb727fee64a63c12df84217cb3a42a82be846921a1bc0a403b52a9",
      "skos:note": "A supporting statement must be in writing and made by a specific person.",
      "dc:description": "details about the practitioner and vulnerable person"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-amendment-strengthening-the-criminal-justice-response-to-sexual-violence-act-2024#sch-1-sec-55-ss-2b",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "55(2B) Subsection 15YR(2)",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 23,
      "values:originalText": "(2B) A supporting statement must:\n(a) be in writing; and\n(b) be made by a person (the practitioner) who is:\n(i) a medical practitioner; or\n(ii) a person registered or licensed as a psychologist under a\nlaw of a State or Territory that provides for the\nregistration or licensing of psychologists; or\n(iii) a person prescribed by the regulations; and\n(c) include the following details:\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\n\nNo. 114, 2024\nCrimes Amendment (Strengthening the Criminal Justice Response to\nSexual Violence) Act 2024\n(i) the name, qualification and business address of the\npractitioner;\n(ii) the nature and duration of the professional relationship\nbetween the practitioner and the vulnerable person; and\n(d) state that the practitioner is of the opinion that the vulnerable\nperson understands:\n(i) what it means to be identified as a vulnerable person of\nthat kind; and\n(ii) the consequences of losing anonymity."
    },
